Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: catalog.c
Line: 3452
Function: xmlCatalogDumpDoc
Bug type: null-pointer-dereference
CWE: CWE-476
Explanation: xmlCatalogDumpDoc unconditionally dereferences xmlDefaultCatalog->xml. However, xmlDefaultCatalog can be NULL after initialization failures: in xmlInitializeCatalog, if xmlCreateNewCatalog returns NULL, xmlDefaultCatalog remains NULL but xmlCatalogInitialized is set to 1. Subsequent calls to xmlCatalogDumpDoc will skip initialization and dereference xmlDefaultCatalog->xml, causing a NULL pointer dereference.

